*Two strikes → blocked.** Same failure twice = stop, log `blocked` with exact error + what you tried. Do not redesign around the contract.\n32\t10. **Small diffs.** Respect the contract's `budget` (changed lines). Over budget = split request via `blocked`, not a big PR.\n33\t\n34\t## Observability & transparency (for the owner)\n35\t\n36\tThe board and log ARE the observability: `git log --oneline -- delivery/` shows all delivery activity;\n37\t`board/BOARD.md` is the kanban at a glance; `board/LOG.md` greps to any task's full history.\n38\tWhen Workstream B lands, LOG.md events migrate to the coordination ledger and the Bridge renders this\n39\tboard live (plan B3 — scrum/kanban lanes). Until then, this file-based board is canonical. Lose nothing.\n40\t\n41\t## Standards in force\n42\t\n43\t- **BDD:** Gherkin (`Given/When/Then`) in every contract's Acceptance section.\n44\t- **TDD:** red→green→refactor, tests named after scenarios.\n45\t- **Agile SDLC:** kanban flow (READY→CLAIMED→VERIFY→DONE, WIP limit 1 per agent); milestones are the\n46\t  sprint-equivalent release trains (see `milestones/`); epics group scope; OKRs steer priority.\n47\t  Retro = the VISION-CHECK note each epic closes with (plan §0.5).\n48\t- **Versioning:** semver per milestone (`milestones/*.md` name the target release).\n49\t- **Definition of Done (every task):** all scenarios green · verify exits 0 · lint/format clean ·\n50\t  allowlist respected · board+log updated · independent verifier confirmed · docs/skills touched if\n51\t  the contract says so.\n52\t\n53\t## Standing approvals (owner-granted, plan rev 11)\n54\t\n55\t- **Backend edits for Workstreams B, G, Q, W** (`server/`, `runtime/`, `commands/`) are pre-approved\n56\t  *within each contract's allowlist* — coordination, atomic leases, SSE, run-event streams, and security\n57\t  remediation are backend-owned by design (root `/AGENTS.md` justification satisfied). No per-PR pause needed.\n58\t- **Canonical backlog location:** `delivery