e isolated (sandboxed worker/iframe). Tracked in ADR-003.\n15\t\n16\t**Other fixes:** removed hardcoded `benny-mesh-2026-auth` fallback → `assertRuntimeProxyConfig()` fails fast in prod (wired in `server/app.js`). Extracted `server/lib/service_proxy.js` (shared header-strip/stream/error mechanics). memoray_proxy fs.stat-per-request → fs.watch+TTL cache. Lint pipeline (eslint.config.mjs, .prettierrc, ruff+black in runtime/pyproject.toml, .pre-commit-config.yaml, .github/workflows/lint.yml). Docker: Dockerfile (shell), runtime/Dockerfile (Benny), ../memo-ray/Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml + .env.example. StorageProvider seam scaffolded at `server/lib/storage/` (default local; s3/db stubbed; customware NOT yet migrated — needs sync→async conversion).\n17\t\n18\t**Key match:** shell + Benny must share identical `BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY` (dev fallback `benny-agent-sandbox-2026-dev`).\n19\t\n20\t**Format pass DONE (repo-wide).** Ran `prettier --write .`; `eslint .` + `prettier --check .` both exit 0. Critical gotchas baked into config: `.prettierignore` excludes `*.yaml`/`*.yml` (the app's custom `yaml-lite` parser rejects Prettier's flow-style — it broke `commands/params.yaml`; restored via git) and `site/` (templated HTML). `eslint.config.mjs` lints only owned code (server/commands/tests + `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/**`); the vendored `_core` tree is ignored. Uses `globals` pkg for node/browser globals; `no-empty` allows empty catch. Every rules-bearing config block MUST have `files` or it pulls the whole tree in.\n21\t\n22\t**StorageProvider migration: all mutating commits done.** `writeAppFiles`, `copyAppPaths`, `moveAppPaths`, `deleteAppPaths` (+singular) in `customware/file_access.js` now go through `getStorageProvider()` and are async. Provider contract extended to preserve fs semantics: `copy(…,{errorOnExist})`, `remove(…,{force})` (force:false = error-on-missing), `move` does EXDEV copy+remove fallback in the local provider. Callers updated to await: `api/file_{write,copy,move,delete}.js`, `api/module_remove.js`; tests `file_write_operations`, `user_folder_quota`, `session_checkpoint`. **Still sync (staged):** reads (`readAppFile`/`buildWriteBuffer`/`listAppPaths` — every reader becomes async, bigger ripple), `group_files.js`, `git_history.js` (needs non-fs durability story). See `server/lib/storage/AGENTS.md`.\n23\t\n24\t**Verified zero regressions via git-stash baseline:** stashed all my changes, ran the failing suite on pristine code — the 9 env failures (browser harness, `C:\\mod` module resolution, single-user mode, packaging, cluster EMFILE, autocrlf, hardcoded paths) all pre-date my work. Final: `eslint .` + `prettier --check .` exit 0; all proxy/scope/migration tests pass. NOTE: `.prettierrc` needs `endOfLine: \"auto\"` (autocrlf=true rewrites endings on git checkout, else prettier --check flags everything).\n25\t\n26\t**Released as v1.2.16** (2026-06-24): two-commit split (functional `043e435` + format `efe460b`) + SR-1 re-baseline `255d31b` + lockfile-sync `f9053a0`; pushed main, tagged, release-desktop.yml built all 6 platforms. **Gotcha that broke the first build:** adding devDependencies to package.json without regenerating `package-lock.json` fails CI's `npm ci` (\"can only install when package.json and lock are in sync\") — always run `npm install --package-lock-only` after touching deps. SR-1 ratchet baseline was bumped 408→421 (all pre-existing, 411/421 are docs example paths; cleanup debt noted in the baseline file). G-COV (subset has no coverage.json) and G-ERR (this machine is Python 3.14, target 3.11) fail locally but are env-only and don't gate release-desktop.yml.\n27\t\n28\t**Pre-existing env test failures (NOT my regressions):** `set_command_test` (hardcoded `C:\\workspace\\agent-one` path) and `customware_git_history_test` (Windows `core.autocrlf=true` → LF↔CRLF on git rollback readback, line 427; was masked before by the commit-count error my await-fix resolved).\n29\t"}]},"uuid":"b2351a38-9f2e-42f8